# The Waypoints tab on a radio that does not know where it is.
#
# A Brick has no GPS of its own, so this is the ordinary state of the tab until the radio it is
# attached to has a fix or a fixed position: the list still has its last row, because there is
# always something to do here, and that row has to explain itself twice - once on its supporting
# line for the reader, and once out loud for whoever pressed A before reading it.

scene demo
nofix

tab waypoints
hold 1400

# A on the row that makes a place. Refused - there is nowhere to put it - and said so, rather
# than the press doing nothing at all, which is what a client looking broken looks like.
key a
hold 2200

# A place somebody else shared, to show what the reason does not displace: the sharer's line
# still belongs to the place, and the range column stays empty because a range needs two points
# and we have one.
waypoint ALFA Ridge repeater | up the fire road, gate code is on the tag
hold 1600
key a
hold 2000
